      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 850 mg to 1,000 mg per dose. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the usual maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **Another regimen.** Tell me the dose and frequency.\n- **1,700 mg PO three times daily as written.** If this is deliberate, confirm it and I'll enter it with a note recording that you verified the dose."
      }
